                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.comment' infers comment structure [based on 'commentstring' option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14).\r\n\r\nMy suggestion would be to create a file 'after/ftplugin/cpp.lua' and put `vim.bo.commentstring = '// %s'` line there.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">'mini.comment' infers comment structure <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14\">based on 'commentstring' option</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My suggestion would be to create a file 'after/ftplugin/cpp.lua' and put <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.bo.commentstring = '// %s'</code> line there.</p>",
            "bodyText": "'mini.comment' infers comment structure based on 'commentstring' option.\nMy suggestion would be to create a file 'after/ftplugin/cpp.lua' and put vim.bo.commentstring = '// %s' line there.",
